        "original_id": "5b86dc8a-df4c-53c2-b7d9-144cc3b43e62",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Selfridges, Harrods, Jack O'Shea's\n- Places: London's Oxford Street, UK, Qatar\n- Topics: retail stores, ownership, contracts, ethical code, foie gras\n\nFacts:\n- Selfridges opened its flagship store on London's Oxford Street on 15 March 1909.\n- Selfridges' flagship store on London's Oxford Street is the second largest shop in the UK after Harrods.\n- Harrods is owned by the state of Qatar.\n- Jack O'Shea's was formerly located in Selfridges.\n- Selfridges terminated Jack O'Shea's contract in 2012 after Jack O'Shea's broke the store's ethical code by selling foie gras.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
